      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done in PS6: switched to `#ifndef SK_IGNORE_ELLIPSIZE_TRUNCATED_LINES` (enabled by default, `BUILD.gn` reverted). Also covered `layout(SK_ScalarInfinity)` when `maxLines` is finite, switched `SkParagraph_EllipsisAfterHardLineBreak` from `UNIX_ONLY_TEST` to `DEF_TEST`, and marked cold `TextLine::createEllipsis` `SK_NEVER_INLINE` so single-caller LTO does not bloat `ParagraphImpl::layout` on `ShortLayout`.\n\nWith the fix enabled, all 20,198 Flutter framework and engine tests pass with 0 regressions, so Flutter needs no `flutter_defines.gni` guard. Across google3 SkParagraph clients (1151 test targets), 1150 have no regressions and 1 golden test (`maxLines\u003d2` text wrapping onto a line ending in `\\n`) now renders the expected ellipsis — so we can pre-land `SK_IGNORE_ELLIPSIZE_TRUNCATED_LINES` in `SkUserConfig.h` before submitting this CL, then update that golden and remove the define after the roll.",
